<title>USA: BONNEVILLE OFFERS NO SURPLUS POWER FOR THURSDAY.</title>
<headline>BONNEVILLE OFFERS NO SURPLUS POWER FOR THURSDAY.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bonneville Power Administration (BPA) did not offer any surplus power for Thursday pre-schedulings, the agency said Wednesday.</p>
<p>A trader at the Portland, Ore.-based power marketing agency said, &quot;We wanted to be conservative. Supplies are going to be tight.&quot;</p>
<p>He attributed the supply tightness to regional power demand along with a typical seasonal decline in flows through hydroelectric power projects.</p>
<p>For today, BPA had offered 200 megawatts of peak, firm power at $20.00 per megawatt hour for Northwest sales and $22.00 for California-Oregon border deliveries.</p>
<p>((--Los Angeles bureau +1 213 955 6761))</p>
</text>
